//
// Phase B runtime seam: host-only rules tests.
//
// Covers the BO liveness allocator (live ranges, slot sharing, the content-keyed
// static pool, the dirty-bit discipline) and runlist aggregation (submission
// grouping, the ELF-vs-xclbin argument ABI, the dispatch vector). The rules they
// check are written down in
// docs/plans/transformer-layer-execution-studies/05b-phase-b-buffer-rules.md.
//
// No NPU and no XRT: BoPool takes its allocator as a callable and the ABI
// binding is tested against a fake run object, so this sits alongside the
// compile-only kernel gate and requires neither `ryzen_ai_npu2` nor `peano`.
// The hardware half of Phase B is `make runlist-gate`, which is not a lit test
// because it needs a device and takes minutes.
//
// The test files carry no framework dependency -- pytest is not installed in the
// sandbox venv -- so they run as plain scripts and print a pass count.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/../llms/shared/infra/test_bo_pool.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=POOL
// POOL: 33/33 passed
//
// `[2026-08-25]` 35 -> 40, item 14's review round (blocking): the ELF is the
// ABI ground truth. `dispatch.elf_arg_count` reads the kernel's buffer-arg
// count from the binary's own .dynsym (numeric names ARE the arg indices) and
// `validate_arg_count` refuses -- BEFORE any device work, at load_and_run, the
// one chokepoint every load path dispatches through -- a call that does not
// match it, in either direction, plus a manifest n_args contradicting its ELF.
// The five pin the parser on synthetic ELFs, both refusal directions (the devq
// 583 unbound-scratch class and its inverse), the stale-manifest clause with
// the manifest-only fallback, and by source that the check precedes
// ensure_loaded and that compile time records n_args.
// RUN: python3 %S/../llms/shared/infra/test_dispatch.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DISPATCH
// DISPATCH: 40/40 passed
//
// `[2026-08-21]` Doc 56 H0: the analytical planner's host gates -- the two golden
// graphs pinned, each model's plan reproducing its shipped ELF sequence / launch
// counts / NPU-CPU split, profiles.skip_reason reproduced over every family, the
// caps cross-checked against the study constants, the tile solver ranked against
// the registry with every mismatch in a named class.
// RUN: python3 %S/../llms/shared/plan/test_plan.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAN
// PLAN: 10/10 passed
//
// `[2026-08-23]` Doc 57 O1 second half: the Qwen3 QKV stage's two host ABIs --
// the driver's argument helper follows QWEN3_RMS_QKV_LAUNCHES, the 2-launch
// shapes, the augmented weight's (tag, kind) per row, the slot gather as the
// inverse of the device's slot layout.
// RUN: python3 %S/../llms/shared/infra/test_decode_qkv4.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=QKV4
// QKV4: 4/4 passed
